  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The formula to calculate the density of the material of the wire is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mrow><msup><mi>&#960;R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Hence, the formula to calculate the percentage error in calculating the density of the material can be written as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>&#961;</mi></mrow><mi>&#961;</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Substitute the values of the known parameters into equation (2) to calculate the required percentage error.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>03</mn></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>04</mn></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>4</mn><mo>%</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p></blockquote>",
